cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software/paper, please cite it as below."
title: "OxAlphaTrace: A Behavioral Fingerprinting Study of a Stealth Language Model"
abstract: "A reproducible, behavior-only investigation of a stealth-served language model (openrouter/stealth/ox-alpha). Benchmarks a near-ceiling capability profile and ranks seven candidate model families via a twelve-probe meta-cognition battery with multi-seed replication, plus a blind-attribution experiment, to assess how far observable behavior can go as a provenance fingerprint."
authors:
  - name: "OxAlphaTrace Working Group"
date-released: "2026-08-23"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - "behavioral fingerprinting"
  - "model attribution"
  - "stealth models"
  - "LLM evaluation"
  - "model provenance"
  - "inter-rater reliability"
